  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ca729eba",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### `Diagonal`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2dbb8ad2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- *np.diag()*: Create a diagonal matrix"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "67444bb1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### What Does `np.diag()` Do?\n",
    "\n",
    "The important thing to know is that `np.diag()` has **two main uses**:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "np.diag()\n",
    "   │\n",
    "   ├── If you give it a 1D array → Creates a diagonal matrix\n",
    "   │\n",
    "   └── If you give it a matrix → Extracts the diagonal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 140,
   "id": "1f4bbdad",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[[1 0 0]\n",
      " [0 2 0]\n",
      " [0 0 3]]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "x = np.array([1, 2, 3])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(np.diag(x))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 141,
   "id": "f4bf5c48",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[1 4]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "A = np.array([\n",
    "    [1, 2],\n",
    "    [3, 4]\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(np.diag(A))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8a7b9e93",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### `Repeat and Tile`"
