  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0ace7244",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### `Broadcasting`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1bce6e6d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### What is Broadcasting?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Broadcasting** is a NumPy feature that allows us to perform operations between arrays with different shapes.\n",
    "\n",
    "NumPy automatically **expands the smaller array** so that it can work with the larger array.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 144,
   "id": "acbe34d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[[11 22 33]\n",
      " [14 25 36]]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "A = np.array([\n",
    "    [1, 2, 3],\n",
    "    [4, 5, 6]\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "x = np.array([10, 20, 30])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(A + x)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "da7efee4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- **Broadcasting does not work with every combination of shapes**\n",
    "    - *The arrays must have compatible shapes*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a4484550",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Axis in NumPy\n",
    "\n",
    "**Axis tells NumPy which direction to perform an operation.**\n",
    "\n",
    "Consider:\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "x = np.array([\n",
    "    [1, 2, 3],\n",
    "    [4, 5, 6]\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "np.sum(x, axis=0)\n",
    "# axis=0 → Down the rows ⬇️\n",
    "# Calculate column by column\n",
    "# Output:\n",
    "    # [5 7 9]\n",
    "\n",
    "np.sum(x, axis=1)\n",
    "# axis=1 → Across the columns ➡️\n",
    "# Calculate row by row:\n",
    "# Output:\n",
    "    # [6 15]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f72e24c8",
   "metadata": {},
